 "notes": [
  "ROYAL COURT (client/scenes/tabs/court.gd), cut from court.png: the header scene with its title and line baked, six cards where the painting has them (the left column's frames x 171..531, the right's 545..911; rows from 487, 843, 1199, 343, 345 and 351 tall -- the painting drifts, and each card keeps its own), and the foot's foliage pinned to the screen's foot.",
  "status_*: the card's live line, in the painting's empty plate. Each plate's inside, measured on its silver rim: x 192..512 on the left and 566..891 on the right; y 770..815, 1129..1173 and 1491..1535. The line is Garamond 26 (the card titles' caps are 18 tall, Cinzel 26) centred on it, 12 units in from each side.",
  "badge_* / count_*: the painting's count disc (court/badge, a gold-ringed red disc 58 across) where each card has it painted -- centres x 496 and 877, y 521, 876 and 1232.5 -- with the count in type (Cinzel 26, as the rail's bubble), drawn only while something waits. The disc is lifted from the card crops.",
  "hit_*: the whole card is the tap; SEASON PASS and CHESTS are dimmed and do nothing until they open."
 ],
